  "comment": "Run: ntfsfix /dev/sdxx This command comes from ntfsprogs. Do be warned (from the man page): ntfsfix is a utility that fixes some common NTFS problems. ntfsfix is NOT a Linux version of chkdsk. It only repairs some fundamental NTFS inconsistencies, resets the NTFS journal file and schedules an NTFS consistency check for the first boot into Windows. Pranala Menarik fsck",
